{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "def check(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer n is one less than twice its digit-reverse.\n    Example: check(1) -> True because 1 == 2 * 1 - 1\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n\n    # Reverse digits via string reversal (handles trailing zeros correctly)\n    reversed_n = int(str(n)[::-1])\n    return n == 2 * reversed_n - 1"}
