{"task_id": "Mbpp/20", "solution": "def is_woodall(value: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is a Woodall number.\n    A Woodall number is of the form n * 2^n - 1 for a non-negative integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"value must be an integer\")\n\n    if value < -1:\n        # Woodall numbers for n >= 0 are always >= -1 (0*2^0 - 1 = -1).\n        return False\n\n    # Practical search bound from design: DEFAULT_MAX_N = 256\n    # n * 2^n grows quickly; search up to this bound.\n    for n in range(0, 257):\n        candidate = n * (1 << n) - 1  # use bit shift for 2**n\n        if candidate == value:\n            return True\n        if candidate > value:\n            return False\n\n    return False"}
