{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of substrings in a digit string where the sum of digits equals the substring's length.\n    Uses a prefix sum approach with a hash map for O(n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    from collections import defaultdict\n\n    pref = 0\n    # counts stores the frequency of (prefix_sum - index) values encountered so far.\n    # Initialize with {0: 1} to account for substrings starting from index 0.\n    counts = defaultdict(int)\n    counts[0] = 1\n    result = 0\n\n    # Convert string s to a list of integers (digits)\n    # The problem description implies valid digit strings for this specific function.\n    digits = [int(char) for char in s]\n\n    for i, digit in enumerate(digits):\n        pref += digit\n        # The key is (current_prefix_sum - current_length), where current_length is (i + 1).\n        # We are looking for previous indices 'j' where (prefix_sum_up_to_j - j) == (current_prefix_sum - current_length).\n        key = pref - (i + 1)\n        result += counts[key]\n        counts[key] += 1\n\n    return result"}
