{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the Eulerian number A(n, m), the number of permutations of {1..n}\n    with exactly m ascents.\n    Uses the recurrence: A(0,0)=1 and\n      A(n,m) = (n-m)*A(n-1,m-1) + (m+1)*A(n-1,m).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not isinstance(m, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n and m must be integers\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n    # By convention A(0,0)=1; for m out of range return 0\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Space-optimized DP: keep only previous row\n    prev = [0] * (n + 1)\n    prev[0] = 1  # A(0,0) = 1\n\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        curr = [0] * (k + 1)\n        for j in range(0, k + 1):\n            left = prev[j - 1] if j > 0 else 0\n            right = prev[j] if j < k else 0\n            curr[j] = (k - j) * left + (j + 1) * right\n        prev = curr\n\n    return prev[m]"}
