{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's in any substring.\n    Uses a Kadane-like algorithm by mapping '0' to +1 and '1' to -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_diff_so_far = -float('inf')\n    current_max_diff = 0\n\n    for char_code in s:\n        # Map '0' to +1, '1' to -1\n        value = 1 if char_code == '0' else -1\n\n        # Kadane's algorithm logic:\n        # If adding the current value to the current sum makes it larger than\n        # starting a new subarray with just the current value, extend the subarray.\n        # Otherwise, start a new subarray.\n        current_max_diff = max(value, current_max_diff + value)\n\n        # Update the overall maximum difference found\n        max_diff_so_far = max(max_diff_so_far, current_max_diff)\n\n    return max_diff_so_far"}
