{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def larg_nnum(items, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a list containing the n largest unique items from the input iterable `items`.\n\n    - Duplicates in `items` are removed (results are unique values).\n    - If n <= 0 an empty list is returned.\n    - If n >= number of distinct items, all distinct items are returned sorted descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    import heapq\n\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Try fast deduplication via set; fallback to order-preserving dedup for unhashable items.\n    try:\n        unique_items = list(set(items))\n    except TypeError:\n        seen = []\n        for x in items:\n            if x not in seen:\n                seen.append(x)\n        unique_items = seen\n\n    if n >= len(unique_items):\n        return sorted(unique_items, reverse=True)\n\n    return heapq.nlargest(n, unique_items)"}
