{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "from typing import Optional\ndef even_bit_set_number(n: int, width: Optional[int] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-position bits (1-based, LSB is position 1) of a number.\n    If width is not provided, it defaults to the bit-length of n (or 1 if n is 0).\n    \"\"\"\n    def _safe_bit_length(val: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the bit length of an integer, handling 0 by returning 1.\"\"\"\n        bl = val.bit_length()\n        return bl if bl > 0 else 1\n\n    effective_width = width\n    if effective_width is None:\n        effective_width = _safe_bit_length(n)\n\n    mask = 0\n    # Iterate through 1-based bit positions up to the effective width\n    for pos in range(1, effective_width + 1):\n        # If the position is even (1-based), set the corresponding bit (0-based) in the mask\n        if pos % 2 == 0:\n            mask |= (1 << (pos - 1))\n\n    return n | mask"}
