{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(pairs):\n    # This function counts occurrences of canonicalized 2-element tuples in a list.\n    counts = {}\n    for pair in pairs:\n        if not (isinstance(pair, (list, tuple)) and len(pair) == 2):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Each item must be a 2-element tuple/list, got: {pair!r}\")\n        a, b = pair\n        try:\n            a_int = int(a)\n            b_int = int(b)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Tuple elements must be integers or convertible to int, got: {pair!r}\")\n        canonical_pair = (a_int, b_int) if a_int <= b_int else (b_int, a_int)\n        counts[canonical_pair] = counts.get(canonical_pair, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
