{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "def combinations_colors(input_list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all combinations with repetition of elements from input_list for a given length n.\n    Returns a list of tuples, where each tuple is a combination.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n\n    if not input_list:\n        # No combinations possible when no elements are provided and n > 0\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    num_elements = len(input_list)\n\n    # Initialize indices for the first combination (all first elements)\n    indices = [0] * n\n\n    while True:\n        current_combination = tuple(input_list[i] for i in indices)\n        result.append(current_combination)\n\n        # Increment indices like an odometer\n        pos = n - 1\n        while pos >= 0:\n            indices[pos] += 1\n            if indices[pos] < num_elements:\n                break\n            indices[pos] = 0\n            pos -= 1\n\n        if pos < 0:\n            break\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than a given non-negative integer n\n    using the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be non-negative\")\n\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0:2] = [False, False]  # 0 and 1 are not prime\n\n    p = 2\n    while p * p < n:\n        if is_prime[p]:\n            # Mark multiples of p as not prime, starting from p*p\n            for multiple in range(p * p, n, p):\n                is_prime[multiple] = False\n        p += 1\n\n    return sum(1 for v in is_prime if v)"}
