{"task_id": "Mbpp/430", "solution": "def parabola_directrix(a: float, b: float, c: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the y-coordinate of the directrix for a parabola y = a x^2 + b x + c.\n    The directrix is given by y = k - p where:\n      h = -b/(2a)\n      k = c - b^2/(4a)\n      p = 1/(4a)\n    Combining: directrix = c - (b^2 + 1) / (4a)\n    \"\"\"\n    four_a = 4.0 * a\n    b_squared = b * b\n    numerator = b_squared + 1.0\n\n    return c - (numerator / four_a)"}
