{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray in the given list of numbers.\n    The algorithm handles positive, negative, and zero values efficiently in a single pass.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        # Based on FR1: input must contain at least one number.\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list must contain at least one number.\")\n\n    max_product_overall = nums[0]\n    current_max_product = nums[0]\n    current_min_product = nums[0]\n\n    for n in nums[1:]:\n        temp_max = current_max_product * n\n        temp_min = current_min_product * n\n\n        current_max_product = max(n, temp_max, temp_min)\n        current_min_product = min(n, temp_max, temp_min)\n\n        max_product_overall = max(max_product_overall, current_max_product)\n\n    return max_product_overall"}
