{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\ndef combinations_list(items: List[Any]) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all possible combinations (power set) of the elements of a given list.\n    Subsets are enumerated by increasing bitmask, and elements within each subset\n    are ordered by descending original index.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(items)\n    result: List[List[Any]] = []\n\n    # Iterate through all possible masks from 0 to 2^n - 1\n    for mask in range(0, 1 << n):\n        subset: List[Any] = []\n        # Construct each subset by iterating indices from n-1 down to 0,\n        # including the item if the corresponding bit in the mask is set.\n        for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n            if (mask >> i) & 1:\n                subset.append(items[i])\n        result.append(subset)\n\n    return result"}
