{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "def first_Digit(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first (most significant) digit of a given number, ignoring sign and decimal parts.\n    Handles ints, floats, and numeric strings. Returns an int in 0..9.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input cannot be None\")\n\n    s = str(n).strip()\n    if s == \"\":\n        raise ValueError(\"Input cannot be empty\")\n\n    # Remove leading sign\n    if s[0] in \"+-\":\n        s = s[1:]\n\n    # Take integer portion if decimal present\n    if \".\" in s:\n        s = s.split(\".\", 1)[0]\n\n    # After removing sign/decimal, treat empty as zero\n    s = s.lstrip(\"0\")\n    if s == \"\":\n        return 0\n\n    if not s.isdigit():\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid numeric input: {n!r}\")\n\n    return int(s[0])"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(nums: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of unordered pairs (i < j) in a list of integers\n    whose XOR sum is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for num in nums:\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    return even_count * odd_count"}
