{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "def merge(matrix):\n    if not matrix:\n        return [[], []]\n\n    firsts = []\n    seconds = []\n    for i, row in enumerate(matrix):\n        if not isinstance(row, (list, tuple)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Row {i} is not a sequence: {row!r}\")\n        if len(row) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Row {i} does not have exactly 2 elements: {row!r}\")\n        firsts.append(row[0])\n        seconds.append(row[1])\n\n    return [firsts, seconds]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/619", "solution": "def move_num(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Moves all numeric characters in the input string to the end, preserving relative order.\n    Non-numeric characters appear first, followed by all numeric characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_digits = []\n    digits = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isdigit():\n            digits.append(char)\n        else:\n            non_digits.append(char)\n    return ''.join(non_digits) + ''.join(digits)"}
