{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(value: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit integer `value` to the left by `d` positions.\n    The rotation operates on the unsigned 32-bit representation of the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_WIDTH = 32\n    MASK = 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    # Normalize the value to its 32-bit unsigned representation\n    v = value & MASK\n\n    # Canonicalize the shift amount\n    s = d % BIT_WIDTH\n\n    if s == 0:\n        return v\n\n    # Perform the left rotation\n    # (v << s) shifts bits left, potentially overflowing the 32-bit boundary.\n    # (v >> (BIT_WIDTH - s)) shifts the overflowing bits from the left back to the right.\n    # The final & MASK ensures the result remains within 32 bits.\n    return ((v << s) | (v >> (BIT_WIDTH - s))) & MASK"}
